  "notes": [
    "Five policies use two separately trained networks per task/model seed, not five separately trained models.",
    "Repair-only runs all nodes. Soft state gating does not skip dense message/update MLPs. Literal old-output selection exists only in gated policies.",
    "Recompute suppresses old-answer/edit features inside the model; Repair consumes them. Both see the modified graph.",
    "R counts recurrent message-passing inference steps, not training epochs. Main table R=8; the same policy also supports longer prefixes.",
    "Each decode includes output normalization and CPU global rooted-path value refresh before later mixing/checks. Counts do not measure all CPU work.",
    "The learned safety score is available after full prefix computation/decode. Eligible reachable non-source nodes with old parents and score>=threshold copy old parent and scalar; others keep the fresh candidate.",
    "The input-only certificate checks reachability/rooted paths/scalars and Bellman inequalities with absolute tolerance1e-5. It does not read new exact labels.",
    "Continue acceptance advances the same pre-mixing neural hidden state/context by8. It does not encode mixed outputs into the hidden state, reapply the old-output mask, or run a second automatic certificate.",
    "Rejection discards the mixed output and starts an independently encoded Recompute8. No second automatic certificate is run on the returned fallback.",
    "model_calls is the recorded independently encoded neural-session counter. Continuing the same session adds an advance and decode, not another model_call.",
    "Equal recurrent steps do not imply equal dense MACs, encoding/decoding counts, decision overhead or time. CopySafe acceptance uses fewer steps by design; formal matched-prefix/depth controls and actual costs must be reported.",
    "The 35 traces are old-weight execution evidence across7 contexts/6 inputs, not new-model accuracy, branch rates or independent graph replicates. The R8 table uses30 traces across6 contexts."
  ]
